@misc{corroboration-negative-search-shared-a-wrong-map,
  section  = {report},
  claim    = {the unrecoverability half of that friction was wrong and this delegate helped make it wrong by over-checking --- told the prose was destroyed, it set out to verify rather than accept, searched git log --all, the stash list, and every dangling BLOB in git fsck --lost-found for the exact headings named, and CONFIRMED the loss in a commit message and a letter; the records were recoverable throughout, because git stash push -u stores untracked files in a parentless commit that git log --all does not list, and the answer sat in the same fsck output already run, on the seven lines reading dangling COMMIT rather than dangling blob, two of which say held: 5 delegate capability records. So the defect was not effort: two independent parties searched, one deliberately over-searching, and both were wrong in the SAME DIRECTION because they shared a wrong model of where the data would be --- decorrelated review is not decorrelated when the reviewers share the modelling error, and searching a different region of one wrong map is not a second opinion. ⚠ The general rule this delegate now holds: when verifying a NEGATIVE, enumerate the output before filtering it and state which regions went unsearched, because I found nothing is a fact about a search while it is not there is a claim about the world, and the first does not license the second},
