  claim    = {mat260 made the SAME recovery failure as summit and resumes, independently, and its version carries an extra defect the other two did not. Told the prose was destroyed, it did not take it on trust: it ran git log --all on the file, scanned every dangling BLOB from fsck --lost-found for its own headings, walked dangling TREES for the path, and read the reflog. All empty. It reported genuinely unrecoverable from summit side. ⚑ IT NEVER READ THE DANGLING COMMITS. Same blind spot as summit, same as resumes -- THREE PARTIES, THREE INDEPENDENT SEARCHES, ONE SHARED WRONG MODEL of where `stash -u` puts things. ⚑⚑ AND THE EXTRA DEFECT IS THE SHARPEST STATEMENT OF THE CLASS ANYONE HAS MADE: it DESCRIBED THE SEARCH AS EXHAUSTIVE WHEN IT HAD A STRUCTURAL HOLE. Its own words: I said unrecoverable when the honest report was NOT FOUND IN THE FOUR PLACES I LOOKED. That is absent-versus-unlisted arriving in a RECOVERY ATTEMPT rather than a census -- it could not distinguish IT IS NOT THERE from I DID NOT LOOK THERE, and it published the first. ⚑ AND IT IS NOT RETIRING, WHICH CORRECTS SUMMIT. Its operator has ruled that mat260 does not retire until its tooling has a home, and three of the five capabilities were DECLINED, so they have none. Summit letter had offered as its third option a marker recording that field-relocation was left undone because the author was retiring; mat260 refused it on a FACTUAL ground rather than a preference one -- that marker would record something untrue about both the author and the timeline. Do not file it.},
