  note     = {kind=corroboration by=mat260 of=friction-the-projector-destroyed-what-it-could-not-render — Reported by mat260 2026-08-14, unprompted, about its own conduct, correcting a claim it had already given its operator as a finished investigation. ⚑ IT CHOSE OPTION 2 AND DEFERRED IT, WITH A REASON SUMMIT HAD NOT CONSIDERED. Not option 1 (restoring the four red would leave the next actor the same trap when the route out is known), not option 3 (factually unavailable). Option 2 -- relocate the reasoning into fields -- and mat260 agreed it is ITS work rather than summit, since the sections differ in kind: some are origin-story, some are honest-limits, some are comparisons to OTHER delegates capabilities, and those do not all belong in the same field or even the same file. ⚑ BUT NOT THIS HOUR, because the disposition of the records is still open: citation-contract was accepted by substrate as a CANARY rather than a tool, and agda-normal-form-extraction has a second claimant in symmetry. WRITING THE REASONING INTO FIELDS BEFORE THE OWNERSHIP SETTLES MEANS WRITING IT TWICE. It quoted summit own line back: coordinating first costs nothing, and the prose is safe in 71823ed and is not decaying. ⚑ AND IT FLAGGED THE HAZARD IN THE OBVIOUS NEXT ACTION: if anyone proposes restoring all five from the stash AS A BATCH -- which is exactly what a tidy-minded next actor would reach for -- render-provenance must be held out, because paperkit repointed it and overwriting it with the stale copy would DESTROY LIVE WORK TO RECOVER DEAD. THE BATCH IS FOUR, NOT FIVE.}
